{"kind":"request","text":"SB-1: a peer read never loads a scope row without a size check.\n\nThe fact at main 694a8c7f. `ScopeObject.nativeBirth`\n(`packages/scope/src/object.ts:810`) calls `#recoverArchiveAlarm`\nbefore it makes its deadline and its `PreparationBudget`. The\nrecovery reads `this.#store.scope()?.status` (`object.ts:450`), and\n`SqliteStore.scope` (`packages/scope/src/sqlite.ts:321`) selects the\nwhole row with no size check. `ArchiveDriver.wake` reads the scope\nthrough the same store. The preparation read of the same row checks\n4096 bytes first (`packages/scope/src/preparation-scope.ts`). A peer\nthat calls `births.read` so makes the sender load and parse a row of\nany size before the sender's budget applies. Fresh-act admission\nand the archive walk of AE-1 both call that read. The builder found\nit in audit 853f63cf.\n\nBefore code, send one act with two answers:\n1. Where the row is written, and what bounds its size at the write.\n   When the write already holds the row under 4096 bytes, a static\n   test of that bound closes this request with no change of the\n   read.\n2. What the recovery does today for a row that the preparation read\n   refuses.\n\nWork, when the write has no such bound:\n1. The recovery reads the status with a size check, at the bound\n   that the preparation read uses. One constant, not two.\n2. For a row over the bound, the recovery does nothing and the peer\n   read answers as the preparation read answers today.\n3. The alarm recovery of a scope with a row in the bound does not\n   change. One witness shows it.\n\nOrder: a small head after AE-1. It does not hold AE-1.","body":{"conditions":"The builder states where the scope row is written and its bound there. Either a static test proves the row stays under the preparation bound, or the recovery reads the status with that one bound and does nothing for a larger row. The alarm recovery of a scope in the bound does not change. Gate passes and the checker reviews the head.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:853f63cfe2a1e529345737514e817ebd12a578b6 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","target_head":"694a8c7f83deedb4e8d34706c51203029726121a","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}